{"kind":"report","text":"APPROVED at exact integration head c234cbf661f37b1af9b95e330886b0a953ece525 (one commit atop the merged release gap closure 094a62e; not on main). Judged against the operator umbrella #2271 verbatim. RELEASED POSIX INSTALLER: the rendered install.sh asset now defaults to installing all five built-in bundles, accepts --bundles LIST and --bundles none, and --interactive only through a readable/writable /dev/tty with no prompt by default; adds --no-service. IN-BINARY SETUP: tailapp setup [--bundles LIST|none] [--interactive] calls apps_list then the create-only app_install control operation for missing built-ins only, never overwriting, activating, or resetting an existing Tailapp, and returns JSON (home, requested, installed, already_present); unknown and duplicate names are refused. USER-OWNED PATHS, NO SUDO, NO TELEMETRY EDITS: install under \u003croot\u003e/lib/tailapp and \u003croot\u003e/bin, home under \u003croot\u003e/share/tailapp, state under \u003croot\u003e/state/tailapp; nothing touches harness settings. SERVICES ON THE CANONICAL HOME: LaunchAgent (validated when present, staged plist, plutil -lint, bootstrap or kickstart) and systemd --user unit on the same TAILAPP_HOME, wait for control-plane health, status and log guidance printed; Linux lingering attempted with an explicit administrator request when it fails. NO USABLE SERVICE MANAGER: the binary and requested bundles are retained (bundles installed through a temporary resident on 127.0.0.1:0), the exact foreground remedy is printed, and the result is nonzero unless --no-service was chosen. HOME DISCREPANCY RESOLVED: Home() now defaults to ~/.local/share/tailapp (defaultHome, tested) instead of os.UserConfigDir()/tailapp, matching the installer, setup script, services, and docs, which state the choice explicitly. TESTS: mocked boundaries - installer end to end against a file:// release with a fake cosign and --bundles none --no-service, plus a fake failing launchctl proving per